module.exports = /*#__PURE__*/JSON.parse('{"participation":{"id":"pulsecheck-program-participation","version":"v1-pulsecheck","category":"participation","title":"Program participation and privacy","body":"PulseCheck supports performance, wellness reflection, and access to support. Licensed professionals remain responsible for clinical decisions and care.\\n\\nParticipation is voluntary. You may decline or stop participating without affecting team status, scholarship, playing time, medical care, academic standing, or your relationship with staff. You can choose whether to share optional wellness responses or connect approved wearables. Contact your program administrator to stop participation.\\n\\nParticipation may include onboarding, performance and wellness check-ins, mental training, conversations with Nora, optional wearable information, and feedback. PulseCheck may collect and retain approved program information to provide these features. Access is limited by role and purpose. Your program’s separate support choices and any required health-information authorization describe what information may be shared with support staff or licensed providers. Clinical notes, diagnoses and treatment records remain in the clinical environment.\\n\\nParticipant data must not be sold or used for unrelated advertising. Restricted clinical or mental-health information must not be used by PulseCheck for independent model training, commercial profiling or unrelated product development. Approved aggregate or properly de-identified information may support program evaluation and permitted product improvement. Identifiable research use requires its own applicable study consent, authorization or waiver and institutional approval.\\n\\nAI responses can be inaccurate. Participation may cause emotional discomfort or involve privacy and security risks. Benefits such as greater self-awareness or easier access to support are possible and are not guaranteed. During an emergency, call 911 or call or text 988, or use your institution’s urgent support resources. Platforms are not emergency response services.\\n\\nA proposed Tier 2 clinical handoff includes a separate choice to accept or decline. Declining that handoff leaves your participation and research choices unchanged. Urgent Tier 3 safety events follow approved institutional procedures and applicable law. Your participation choice does not authorize every disclosure. Health-information authorization, where required, and optional research are separate decisions. You retain your legal rights."},"health":{"id":"pulsecheck-health-authorization","version":"v1-pulsecheck","category":"health_authorization","title":"Health information sharing authorization","body":"This is a separate choice from joining your program. This authorization applies where HIPAA applies and authorization is required. You may authorize or decline. Declining limits only functions that require this authorization.\\n\\nInformation: approved onboarding answers about wellness, stress, sleep, emotional well-being and safety; approved wearable and recovery information; and the concern summary needed for your clinical handoff.\\n\\nWho may disclose: Pulse Intelligence Labs, your institution’s authorized health or counseling personnel, and licensed providers involved in your support, for information each lawfully maintains. Recipients: authorized institutional health or counseling personnel and licensed providers involved in your support. Purpose: approved onboarding transfer, care navigation and clinical-support workflows. Clinical notes, diagnoses and treatment records remain in the clinical environment. Coaches receive only information permitted for their role.\\n\\nPulse may collect and retain approved program information and transmit designated information. Restricted clinical information must not be used for independent model training, commercial profiling, advertising or unrelated product development. This authorization excludes optional research.\\n\\nThis authorization expires when your program participation ends. You may revoke it in writing through your program’s designated privacy contact or send a request to tre@fitwithpulse.ai for routing to the responsible privacy team. Revocation applies to future uses that rely on this authorization; prior reliance and uses otherwise permitted or required by law are unaffected. Your medical care, benefits, scholarship, team status, playing time and academic standing remain unaffected by your decision. Disclosed information may be redisclosed and may cease to be protected by HIPAA, while other protections may still apply. You can save a copy of your decision and these terms. Tier 2 support also asks for your event-specific choice. Urgent safety events follow the approved institutional protocol and applicable law."}}');

